# API test conventions

Specs live under `api/` and follow `api/CATALOG.md`. Shared pieces: `api/fixtures.ts`, `api/helpers/catalog-response.ts`, `support/api.constants.ts`, `support/api-client.ts`.

**Documented** = spec or approved doc. **Observed** = catalog row after you capture traffic (add or update the row). Anything else → **Not yet tested** in `api/CATALOG.md`. Observed rows → characterization tests; a given formal spec → contract tests.

## 1. Sources of truth

✅ **Good** — executed catalog row; spec pins that row via shared helpers (`api/me.api.spec.ts`):

```typescript
const body = await readCatalogGetJson(await mainApi.get(API_ME));
assertMeBody(body);
```

❌ **Bad** — treat **inspected only** / no undo as ready for a write spec, or mislabel observed probes as “contract” from a spec:

```markdown
| POST | `/api/v1/auth/register` | … | no (no undo observed in this catalog pass) | inspected only |
```

Also: catalog **Not yet tested** says no 4xx were triggered, yet 401 without `Authorization` was observed (`CATALOG_UNAUTHENTICATED_STATUS`) — that is characterization, not a spec contract. Do not invent error JSON shape until observed.

## 2. Requests

`baseURL` from Playwright config (`APP_URL` via `support/api-client.ts`). Use **`mainApi`**, **`altApi`**, **`guestApi`** from `api/fixtures.ts` only. No Bearer token, origin URL, or resource id literals in specs.

✅ **Good** — path constants + id from a prior response (`api/communities.api.spec.ts`):

```typescript
await mainApi.get(API_COMMUNITIES);
await mainApi.get(apiCommunityPath(firstId));
await guestApi.get(API_ME);
```

❌ **Bad** — paste catalog capture mechanics into a spec:

```markdown
Authorization: Bearer (`bt_token`) from localStorage, storageState `playwright/.auth/user.json`
```

## 3. Two tests per endpoint

Per route: one **success** test (status, JSON, catalog fields via `readCatalogGetJson` / `assert*`) and one **intentional error** test that changes exactly one thing (drop auth, omit a required field, empty body). Assert status; assert body shape on errors only when observed. On success, assert catalog fields — not unbounded sensitive dumps.

✅ **Good** — paired success + missing token (`api/me.api.spec.ts`, `api/availability.api.spec.ts`):

```typescript
test('GET /api/v1/me without token returns 401', { tag: '@api' }, async ({ guestApi }) => {
  expect((await guestApi.get(API_ME)).status()).toBe(CATALOG_UNAUTHENTICATED_STATUS);
});
```

❌ **Bad** — `POST /api/v1/children`: one happy path, no sibling that only drops the token / sends invalid or empty body (`api/children.api.spec.ts`):

```typescript
test('POST /api/v1/children create appears on GET /api/v1/me then DELETE removes child', { tag: '@api' }, async ({
  mainApi,
}) => { /* createChild, GET /me, deleteChild — no separate error test for POST */ });
```

## 4. Writes

Only when undo is **documented** or **observed** in the catalog (e.g. `DELETE /api/v1/children/{id}`). Call **`trackRecord`** immediately after create so cleanup runs if the test fails.

✅ **Good** — `api/children.api.spec.ts` after `createChild`:

```typescript
trackRecord({ type: TrackedRecordType.Child, id: created.id, owner: 'main' });
```

Use `catalogChildPayload()`, not inline ids.

❌ **Bad** — catalog says no safe test without undo — do not POST in specs until the row allows it (same register row as §1).

## 5. Tags

Exactly one tag per `test()`: **`@api`**. Never on `describe()`.

✅ **Good** — every spec under `api/` (`api/connections.api.spec.ts`):

```typescript
test('GET /api/v1/connections returns catalog status, JSON, and item shape', { tag: '@api' }, async ({
  mainApi,
}) => { /* … */ });
```

❌ **Bad** — omit the tag (not present in `api/` today; do not add tests this way):

```typescript
test('POST /api/v1/children create appears on GET /api/v1/me then DELETE removes child', async ({
  mainApi,
}) => { /* … */ });
```

When splitting flows into multiple tests, each keeps `{ tag: '@api' }` alone — no `@smoke` / `@e2e`, no tag on `describe()`.

## 6. Evidence

Label every claim **executed**, **inspected only**, or **not yet tested** (catalog `evidence` column and § Not yet tested). Status codes and field lists from a PDF, chat, or agent guess are not evidence until observed.

✅ **Good** — constant tied to catalog probes (`api/helpers/catalog-response.ts`):

```typescript
/** Status observed without `Authorization` on catalog GET probes (2026-10-16). */
export const CATALOG_UNAUTHENTICATED_STATUS = 401;
```

Plus executed row, e.g. `GET /api/v1/me` → `executed` in `api/CATALOG.md`, asserted in `me.api.spec.ts`.

❌ **Bad** — assert harness types from an **inspected only** row, not an executed body:

```markdown
| POST | `/api/v1/auth/register` | … | `parent`, `token` (per `parseRegisterResponse`) | inspected only |
```

Do not fill **Not yet tested** (error JSON shape, expired JWT, sign-in path) from prediction.
